From: Kenneth Chan <kenneth.t.chan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: do not set HCI_LP_PARK

Unisoc UWE5622 rejects the default link policy when PARK is included
and hciattach never finishes setup. hci_setup_link_policy must not
set HCI_LP_PARK.

---
 net/bluetooth/hci_core.c | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/bluetooth/hci_core.c b/net/bluetooth/hci_core.c
--- a/net/bluetooth/hci_core.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/hci_core.c
@@ -511,8 +511,6 @@ static void hci_setup_link_policy(struct hci_request *req)
 		link_policy |= HCI_LP_HOLD;
 	if (lmp_sniff_capable(hdev))
 		link_policy |= HCI_LP_SNIFF;
-	if (lmp_park_capable(hdev))
-		link_policy |= HCI_LP_PARK;
 
 	cp.policy = cpu_to_le16(link_policy);
 	hci_req_add(req, HCI_OP_WRITE_DEF_LINK_POLICY, sizeof(cp), &cp);
